{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Elohim blessed</b> — Three instances of juxtaposed (construct) forms in the Masorah: here, and the second: ויברך אלהים את נח, and the third: ויברך אלהים את יצחק. When He created the world He blessed Shabbat and the world. In the days of Noah, when all the first ones were destroyed and the world was renewed, it needed blessing a second time. And He blessed Yitzchak, as in the Midrash: \"Until now I needed to bless My creations; from here onward the blessings are placed in your hand.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:30.523158296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}